            <ArticleTitle>Ergonovine provocation in post partum myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>110-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Post-partum myocardial infarction is rare and the pathophysiology obscure. This report describes a 30-year-old lactating female in whom an inferolateral wall myocardial infarction was documented 5 months following a normal pregnancy and delivery. Coronary angiography revealed normal coronary arteries, a finding described previously in 3 such patients. Contrary to previous speculations, however, provocative testing with ergonovine produced no evidence of coronary artery spasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
